Dear Daofeng

searching for tissue-specific genes is a somewhat different question 
from looking for differential expression.

Many other people may have many different suggestions (and could post 
them here), but a useful starting point for you could be this paper: 
http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3154617/?tool=pubmed#SD1 A 
Gene Expression Barcode for Microarray Data by Michael Zilliox and 
Rafael Irizarry.

In fact, this should be much easier with RNA-Seq data than for 
microarrays. For visualisation / data exploration / density estimation, 
DESeq's variance stabilising transformation could be useful.

	Best wishes
	Wolfgang

